out.push(h2('6.7  Review & Mediate: The reader who has eleven of them'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready – Unit 6 quiz'));
out.push(A('**1** _…the latter **has** not been produced._ **2** _…and I **did so**._ **3** _…fifty-five **are** below the specified grade._ **4** _The old prep room, on the first floor at the east end, **is** to be refloored._ _(and the premodified version goes with the error)_ **5** _There is a requirement for **every** record to be retained for two years_ — **better:** _every record must be kept for two years._ **6** _…the two figures **that** matter are in paragraph 2._'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**b** ⚠ **_How many facts are in the eleven pages?_** **Two pages cannot answer the chairman\'s question, because a two-page summary of a padded report is a padded summary and he cannot tell those apart either.**'));
out.push(A('_(No Practise line in x.7. The Language box in a Review & Mediate cycle collects the moves and carries no Practise item — the house pattern at every level of this series.)_'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the fifth mediation and the first in which neither party is wrong about anything, and the class should be told so before Stage 3.** **In 1.7 a reader had misread; in 3.7 a reader was wrong about the instruction; in 5.7 a writer had put her best sentence second.** **Here the author was asked for every section over four years and the chairman has four hours** — **both facts are true and the problem is arithmetic.** **The first move is therefore unusually easy and unusually important: say to both of them that they are right.** ⚠ **And then the question, which is a question and not an accusation: how many facts are in the eleven pages?** **A writer who is told their report is padded defends it.** **A writer who counts finds the empty paragraphs themselves**, and nobody ever mentions it again.'));
out.push(A('**The fourth move is now standard and the class should be shown the pattern across the book.** ⚠ **1.7, 3.7 and 5.7 had a reader with nothing to do, and the instruction was to leave that reader alone.** **4.7, 6.7 and everything after have a reader who acts, and a reader who acts gets exactly one question.** **Here it is one sentence about the chairman\'s own request** — _two pages will not tell you what you want to know_ — **and then silence.** **He asks what will, and at that point you have been asked and may answer.** **Volunteering the fact count to the chairman before he asks turns the mediation into advice**, and a chairman who has been advised will test the advice rather than use it.'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Pair A, the district report)'));
